# Start the redis-a and redis-b profiles. Use the same Demo__DataFile and Demo__CachePrefix on both.
# For a fresh run, POST /demo/reset before the first GET.
@a = http://localhost:5081
@b = http://localhost:5082

### 1. A queries SQLite and writes L1/L2
GET {{a}}/products/1

### 2. B reads Redis: zero database reads on B so far
GET {{b}}/products/1

### 3. Cache a second product on A
GET {{a}}/products/2

### 4. Cache that same product on B from Redis
GET {{b}}/products/2

### 5. Cache a list on B
GET {{b}}/products?category=keyboards

### 6. A changes product 1; the backplane invalidates it and the lists on B
PUT {{a}}/products/1/price
Content-Type: application/json

{ "price": 119 }

### 7. Product 2 on B is still cached
GET {{b}}/products/2

### 8. Product 1 on B is fresh
GET {{b}}/products/1

### 9. The list on B also contains the new price
GET {{b}}/products?category=keyboards

### 10. A's real database reads
GET {{a}}/demo/queries

### 11. B's real database reads
GET {{b}}/demo/queries

### 12. Remaining entries on B
GET {{b}}/methodcache/entries

### 13. A's health (Degraded after a Redis failure is observed)
GET {{a}}/health

### 14. B's health
GET {{b}}/health
